<title>INDIA: India's reserves cross $19 bln - Chidambaram.</title>
<headline>India's reserves cross $19 bln - Chidambaram.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian Finance Minister P. Chidambaram said on Tuesday the country's foreign reserves crossed $19 billion last week.</p>
<p>He was speaking at a economic editors' conference.</p>
<p>On Saturday, the Reserve Bank of India said foreign currency assets as on October 31, 1996 totalled $19.16 billion against $17.04 billion as on March 31, 1996.</p>
</text>
